{{User:MiszaBot/config
| algo                = old(60d)
| archive             = User talk:ParamBot/Archive %(counter)d
| counter             = 1
| maxarchivesize      = 150K
| archiveheader       = {{Archive}}
| minthreadstoarchive = 1
| minthreadsleft      = 4
}}
{{tmbox
| type = notice
| text = '''This is the talk page of [[User:ParamBot|ParamBot]]''', a bot run by [[User:Phuzion|Phuzion]] and [[User:Zackmann08|Zackmann08]]. When an old, deprecated infobox parameter comes back into an article, it puts the new name back. Both operators watch this page.
* '''Is it making bad edits?''' Change [[User:ParamBot/Run]] to <code>no</code>, and it stops straight away. Then say what happened below. ''A message on this page does not stop the bot.''
* '''Was one edit wrong?''' Revert it, and [{{fullurl:User talk:ParamBot|action=edit&section=new}} start a new section] with a link to the diff. The bot won't edit that article again for 30 days. To keep it off an article for good, add {{tlx|bots|deny{{=}}ParamBot}}.
* '''Why did it edit this article?''' See the [[User:ParamBot/FAQ|FAQ]]. The ''rules'' link in each edit summary shows exactly which rules it used.
* '''Want it to handle another template?''' Follow [[User:ParamBot/Rules/Instructions|the instructions]], or ask below.
* '''Anything else''' is in the [[User:ParamBot/Documentation|documentation]]. The latest run's report is at [[User:ParamBot/Report]].
}}
